ad_svc.trace and connection_trace.txt were written for these tests, in
AnyDesk's formats as real lines published in a CTF write-up show them
(bi0sCTF 2024, "verboten"), with example addresses and made-up IDs. Under
this crate's licences.

wer/lsass/Report.wer and wer/notepad/Report.wer were written for these
tests as Windows Error Reporting writes reports (UTF-16 with a byte order
mark, Name=Value lines), with made-up identifiers. Under this crate's
licences.

screenconnect/ (system.config, user.config, Session.db, deleted.tsv) was
written for these tests by screenconnect/make.py; no openly licensed
ScreenConnect files were found. The settings files follow the .NET
settings layout public scripts read from real clients; Session.db has the
tables and columns ScreenConnect's documentation and reports name, with
assumed column types (ConnectWise doesn't publish its schema). Made-up
names, identifiers and documentation-range addresses. Under this crate's
licences.
